    "title": "http: response dropped when client half-closes after sending request (request still executed)",
    "body": "### Is there an existing issue for this?\n\n- [x] I have searched the existing issues\n\n### Current behaviour\n\nWith the new HTTP server (#35182), if a client sends a complete request and then half-closes its write side (`shutdown(SHUT_WR)`, i.e. sends FIN), the server closes the connection without writing a response. The request is still executed.\n\nSome tools (nc -N, socat) rely on it. Was the change intentional?\n\nThis was found while testing v32.0rc\n\n### Expected behaviour\n\nThe server should write the response and then close, as v31 (libevent) did.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```sh\nbitcoind -regtest -daemon\npython3 -c '\n  import socket, sys\n  s = socket.create_connection((\"127.0.0.1\", 18443))\n  s.sendall(b\"GET / HTTP/1.1\\r\\nHost: x\\r\\n\\r\\n\")\n  s.shutdown(socket.SHUT_WR)\n  while (d := s.recv(4096)): sys.stdout.buffer.write(d)\n'\n```\n\nThis on v32rc gives no output.\n\nOn v31 it does:\n\n```\nBitcoin Core starting\nHTTP/1.1 405 Method Not Allowed\nDate: Wed, 07 Oct 2026 18:57:26 GMT\nContent-Length: 41\nContent-Type: text/html; charset=ISO-8859-1\n\nJSONRPC server handles only POST requests⏎ \n```\n\n### Relevant log output\n\n_No response_\n\n### How did you obtain Bitcoin Core\n\nCompiled from source\n\n### What version of Bitcoin Core are you using?\n\n9dfde64cc3262329051fd05fffe40eecc786a99f\n\n### Operating system and version\n\nArch Linux, kernel 7.1.8-arch1-3\n\n### Machine specifications\n\n_No response_",
