      "body": " I followed the reproduce steps and on v32.0rc there was no output , on v31  i got the following output\n```\nHTTP/1.1 405 Method Not Allowed\nDate: Wed, 07 Oct 2026 21:24:35 GMT\nContent-Length: 41\nContent-Type: text/html; charset=ISO-8859-1\n\nJSONRPC server handles only POST requests\n```\nI tried adding a check in HTTPRemoteClient::MaybeDisconnect that checks if the client is marked for disconnect while a request is still running or a reply is still queued and then keeps the connection until a reply is sent.\n\n`if (m_disconnect && (m_req_busy || ReadyToSend())) return false;`\n\nHere is the link to the commit i made [http: send reply before disconnect on client half-close](https://github.com/tumutech/bitcoin/commit/594886654d1c9bc2b0fc350097116f5b4d738e3f)\n\nIs this approach acceptable? I have tested it out and it returned the response below instead of a blank output after running this test.\nTest run: \n\n`bitcoind -regtest -daemon`\n```\npython3 -c '\nimport socket, sys\ns = socket.create_connection((\"127.0.0.1\", 18443))\ns.sendall(b\"GET / HTTP/1.1\\r\\nHost: x\\r\\n\\r\\n\")\ns.shutdown(socket.SHUT_WR)\nwhile (d := s.recv(4096)): sys.stdout.buffer.write(d)\n'\n```\nOutput: \n`Bitcoin Core starting`\n\n```\nHTTP/1.1 405 Method Not Allowed\nDate: Wed, 07 Oct 2026 23:06:48 GMT\nContent-Length: 41\nContent-Type: text/html; charset=ISO-8859-1\n\nJSONRPC server handles only POST requests\n```\n\n",
